# Copy to `.env` and edit. Nothing here is required to run the app: with an
# empty file it boots fully public, reports nothing to the hub, and serves
# every documentation page. Each block below says what turns ON when you set
# it, and what the app does when you don't.
#
# `.env` is gitignored and excluded from the Docker image (.dockerignore) —
# never bake a developer's copy into a production build. On Render, set these
# in the dashboard rather than committing a file; render.yaml documents the
# production values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# flask | fastapi | quart. FastAPI is the local default (run.py); the Docker
# image pins flask because gunicorn serves WSGI. See lib/backend.py.
# DASH_BACKEND=fastapi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin (lib/constants.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drives <link rel="canonical">, sitemap.xml and the absolute URLs in
# llms.txt. Both names are honoured, one value — APP_BASE_URL (the
# network-wide spelling) wins. In production (RENDER set, or
# APP_ENV=production) the boot REFUSES unless one of them is set:
# see require_owned_base_url() in lib/constants.py.
# APP_BASE_URL=https://emojimart.2plot.dev
# DASH_EMOJI_MART_BASE_URL=https://emojimart.2plot.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2plot network analytics (lib/satellite_reporter.py, lib/traffic_rollup.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The shared HMAC secret every satellite holds (same value as on 2plot.ai).
# Without it the app serves normally and reports nothing.
# CROSS_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# The series this app reports under — its key in the hub's network directory.
# SATELLITE_APP_KEY=emojimart
# The visitor ledger traffic_rollup reads. Production points this at the
# mounted disk (see render.yaml); locally the repo-root default is fine.
# TRAFFIC_ANALYTICS_FILE=/var/data/visitor_analytics.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Corpus document tiers (lib/page_tiers.py; registered in run.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access tier for the tiered corpus documents served by dash-improve-my-llms
# >= 2.4.0: /llms-small.txt (compact briefing) and /llms-full.txt (every
# page's prose in one fetch). Values: public | auth | admin | hidden.
# Unset = public — the network's standing policy is that discovery documents
# stay free; these knobs exist so the 402 experiment can tighten the full
# corpus per-satellite without a redeploy of anything else. The hub's
# page-tier ceilings can also tighten either network-wide (a satellite can
# never loosen below the hub). Inert on older package versions.
# LLMS_SMALL_TIER=public
# LLMS_FULL_TIER=public

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Iconify (dash_emoji_mart.iconify)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the /iconify page caches Iconify API responses (24h TTL). Production
# points at the mounted disk; locally the default temp dir is fine.
# DASH_EMOJI_MART_CACHE_DIR=/var/data/iconify-cache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The interactive gate (lib/access.py, lib/gate_layouts.py, lib/auth.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FLIP LEVER. Every page whose frontmatter declares no `tier` resolves to
# this. Values: public | auth | admin | hidden. Unset = public, which is also
# what production sets explicitly — see render.yaml for why the explicit
# setting matters (its presence forces the access wiring on, so the verdict
# plumbing is live during the dark launch rather than first exercised at the
# moment of a flip).
#
# Rollback from a gated site is this one value, and nothing else.
# PAGE_DEFAULT_TIER=public

# The SECOND axis. While "1", machine surfaces — the llms.txt family, crawler
# HTML, the prerender — stay open even on pages the interactive gate closes,
# which is what keeps the crawl-demand measurement running while humans meet a
# sign-in card. "0" closes the machine lane everywhere at once (the phase-4
# agent flip). Unset = open.
# LLMS_PUBLIC_DEFAULT=1

# The control board's override store (pages/control_board.py). Production
# points this at the mounted disk alongside TRAFFIC_ANALYTICS_FILE; a board
# toggle that resets on every deploy silently republishes a page somebody
# deliberately hid. Its absence is one of the two things the [visibility] boot
# guard warns about.
# PAGE_VISIBILITY_FILE=/var/data/page_visibility.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clerk satellite auth (lib/auth.py) — FULLY OPTIONAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# With no CLERK_* keys, lib/auth.py registers nothing and the site runs fully
# public. That is the default and how this host ships today; the block exists
# so the flip is an environment change and not a redeploy.
#
# Locally, leave CLERK_IS_SATELLITE false — Clerk rejects a satellite whose
# domain it does not recognise, and 127.0.0.1 is not a registered subdomain.
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_...
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_...
# CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=https://accounts.2plot.ai/sign-in
# CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=https://accounts.2plot.ai/sign-up
# Where an authenticated reader lands after signing in from this satellite.
# Unset strands them on the primary, silently; a truthy non-URL renders a Sign
# In button that 404s. lib/auth.py boot-guards both — the absence of its two
# [auth] warnings from a deploy log is an acceptance check, not a nicety.
# CLERK_SATELLITE_SIGN_IN_REDIRECT=https://2plot.ai/onboarding
# REQUIRED in satellite mode; cannot be derived from CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL on a
# production custom-domain instance.
# CLERK_FRONTEND_API=https://clerk.2plot.ai
# The REGISTERED satellite domain, host only — deliberately NOT this app's own
# host. Every *.2plot.dev docs site is an allowed SUBDOMAIN of this one.
# CLERK_SATELLITE_DOMAIN=2plot.dev
# CLERK_IS_SATELLITE=true
# Signs the session and __dca_identity cookies. Without it dash-clerk-auth
# falls back to a PUBLIC dev default. Unique per service, never shared.
# SESSION_SECRET=
# Comma-separated allowlist for admin-tier pages (/admin/control-board).
# ADMIN_EMAILS=
